# Line-ending & binary policy.
#
# Verified 2026-08-26: the index holds 0 CRLF/mixed blobs (`git ls-files --eol`),
# so introducing this file produces NO renormalization diff — it pins the all-LF
# state the repo already has, against a contributor whose core.autocrlf differs
# (Windows defaults to autocrlf=true; every blob here is already LF).

# Default: let git detect text vs binary, normalize text to LF in the repo, and
# convert to the platform's native ending on checkout.
* text=auto

# Must stay LF even on a Windows checkout (shebang / bash correctness), whatever a
# contributor's core.autocrlf is. None committed today; this is future-proofing.
*.sh     text eol=lf

# A LICENSE is a planned addition (founder to-do). Keep it byte-stable LF.
LICENSE* text eol=lf

# Binaries. None are committed today, but this is a web app that will add images
# and OG/social assets. Marking them binary removes any ambiguity: a mis-normalized
# binary corrupts silently and fails when SERVED, not when committed.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.avif   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.wasm   binary
*.pdf    binary

# Migrations (apps/api/migrations/*.sql) need no special pin: node-pg-migrate
# tracks applied migrations by NAME, not by a content hash, and nothing in this
# repo byte-compares them — the `* text=auto` LF normalization above is sufficient
# and does not affect migration tracking.
